-- Rollback 0051 — drop the one-live-subscription-per-workspace index.
--
-- Pure constraint removal: no data is read, written, or destroyed, and
-- no application behaviour depends on the index existing (the app-level
-- `SUBSCRIPTION_EXISTS` guard in billing.service.ts predates it and is
-- untouched). Rolling back simply restores the pre-0051 situation where
-- two concurrent cross-device checkouts could both land a live row.
--
-- Re-applying 0051 afterwards will FAIL if a duplicate slipped in
-- during the rollback window — which is the correct signal, not a bug:
-- deciding which of two live subscriptions survives is a billing
-- decision. Pre-flight before re-applying:
--
--   SELECT workspace_id, count(*) FROM subscriptions
--   WHERE status IN ('active','past_due','paused')
--   GROUP BY 1 HAVING count(*) > 1;

DROP INDEX IF EXISTS "subscriptions_one_live_per_workspace_uniq";
